// (throw immediately vs. return R_UnboundValue) for the null-callback case.
// Returning R_UnboundValue is the safer choice: it lets the existing
// compat_getVar error-handling path at line 23-24 fire through the standard
// Rf_error -> RError chain, producing a legible Python-facing error message
// that includes the symbol name.
